$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Compound 20. Under nitrogen and anhydrous conditions, acid
19 (1.62 mg, 6.20 mmol) was dissolved in dichloroethane (60 mL). POCl3
(2.9 mL, 31.0 mmol) was added, and the solution was brought to reflux for
4 h. Afterward, the solution was concentrated and the residue was dried
under vacuum. Following this, the residue was dissolved in pyridine (60
mL) and aniline linker 18 (2.967 g, 9.30 mmol) was added. The mixture was
stirred overnight at room temperature. The solvent was evaporated, and
the crude solid was dissolved in DCM and washed with 0.1 M HCl and brine.
The solution was dried with MgSO4, which was removed through filtration,
and the solution was concentrated to dryness. The crude product was
purified by flash chromatography in 7:3 hexanes/ethyl acetate. A yellow
solid (1.23 g, 2.23 mmol) was obtained with a 36% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ (ppm) 10.92 (s, 1H), 8.78 (s, 1H), 7.65 (s, 1H), 7.64 (s, 1H),
7.46 (d, J = 9.01 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (t, J = 8.13 Hz, 1H), 6.90 (d, J = 8.23
Hz, 1H), 6.68 (dd, J = 9.01, 2.25 Hz, 1H), 6.53 (d, J = 2.06 Hz, 1H),
3.47 (q, J = 7.05 Hz, 4H), 1.43 (s, 18H), 1.26 (t, J = 7.10 Hz, 6H). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 163.1, 161.1, 157.8, 152.9, 151.8, 148.6,
139.9, 138.8, 131.3, 128.9, 123.6, 119.9, 119.1, 110.2, 110.1, 108.6,
96.6, 82.7, 45.2, 27.9, 12.4. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for C30H37N3O7Na
([MNa+]): 574.2529. Found: 574.2571. Mp: 170.7 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
