$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure V: synthesis of
intermediates 17a-d To a stirred suspension of the carboxylic acid
derivative (1 eq) in DCM (2 mL / mmol carboxylic acid), TBTU (1.1 eq) and
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (2 eq) were added, followed by the
corresponding amine (1 eq). The clear solution was stirred at room
temperature until either TLC or HPLC confirmed complete conversion. The
occurring precipitate was collected by filtration, washed with DCM and
purified by silica flash-chromatography. 4-Bromo-N-cyclopropylbenzamide
(17a) 3-Bromo-N-cyclopropylbenzamide (17b) 17b was synthesized according
to general procedure V. Eluent: ethyl acetate/n-hexane 80/20 → ethyl
acetate/n-hexane 50/50 afforded 91 % yield as a white solid. 1H NMR (200
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.91-7.82 (m, 1H), 7.70-7.54 (m, 2H), 7.34-7.20 (m, 1H),
6.42 (s, 1H), 2.96-2.80 (m, 1H), 0.94-0.77 (m, 2H), 0.70-0.55 (m, 2H).
FAB-MS (m/z): 240/242 [M+H]+.
