$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-benzyl-2-(1H-indol-3-yl)acetamide To a 250 mL round-bottom flask
containing 3-indoleaceticacid (20 mmol, 1.00 equiv), benzylamine (22
mmol, 1.10 equiv) and EDCI (4.217 g, 22 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was added CH2Cl2
(150 mL), followed by DIPEA (7.7 mL, 44 mmol, 2.2 equiv) at 0 ºC. The
mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred overnight.
The reaction was diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed subsequently with 1 M HCl
(aq.), sat. NaHCO3. The aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2x100
mL) and the combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The crude off-white solid can be recrystallized from CH2Cl2
and provided the amide in 75-90% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
